      Height","comment":null,"color":{"r":0.9882354,"g":0.6627451,"b":0.2745098,"a":1.0},"guid":"79679052-0c1b-4b80-b4df-c2c93b524936","$version":"A","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.GraphGroup"},{"position":{"xMin":-5835.0,"yMin":105.0,"xMax":-5014.0,"yMax":495.0},"label":"Drag","comment":null,"color":{"r":0.3764706,"g":0.8862746,"b":0.654902,"a":1.0},"guid":"478c1938-eb15-4f25-94fb-570c517c3768","$version":"A","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.GraphGroup"},{"position":{"xMin":-6575.0,"yMin":-799.0,"xMax":-5313.0,"yMax":-345.0},"label":"Input
      Scale","comment":null,"color":{"r":0.5176471,"g":0.7254902,"b":0.854902,"a":1.0},"guid":"06e25319-993b-4b42-9959-e9c8da3dafa2","$version":"A","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.GraphGroup"},{"position":{"xMin":-5749.0,"yMin":880.0001,"xMax":-2791.999,"yMax":1693.0},"label":"Dash","comment":null,"color":{"r":0.4745098,"g":0.8784314,"b":0.8901961,"a":1.0},"guid":"498e68bd-e424-4e4a-9732-d4b70c58bb55","$version":"A","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.GraphGroup"},{"position":{"xMin":-4567.0,"yMin":194.0,"xMax":-3671.0,"yMax":680.0},"label":"Gravity","comment":null,"color":{"r":0.9803922,"g":0.7686275,"b":0.9490197,"a":1.0},"guid":"11094a4d-5c6e-4fd9-b254-dad34028b313","$version":"A","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.GraphGroup"},{"position":{"xMin":-3514.0,"yMin":-508.0,"xMax":-3350.0,"yMax":-428.0},"title":"Movement","body":"Add
      a count to the number of jumps and turn off the jump button.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"94bf0010-fe68-4eed-9c8c-b064660906f7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4081.0,"yMin":-197.0,"xMax":-3956.0,"yMax":-116.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player can''t jump, check if they''re grounded.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"66af41e6-5c38-4c38-a27b-889ab05fbed7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5153.0,"yMin":1856.0,"xMax":-4837.0,"yMax":1996.0},"title":"Define
      Box","body":"This little bit creates the box that checks if there is floor.
      All the values are hardcoded but you can see the box if you turn on the visualiser
      object. It gets the size of the player''s box, shrinks it down in the x and
      z directions by a little bit (so you can''t cheese it by pressing against a
      wall), then shrinks down the y and shifts it down by a lot for the same reason.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"40dbe553-7740-4d6c-a13d-2f868295bd3b","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5261.0,"yMin":-1322.0,"xMax":-5061.0,"yMax":-1230.0},"title":"Z-Lock","body":"Stop
      the player from falling off the front or back of the map by constantly setting
      its Z position to 0, the centre of the world.","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"c13976e4-772e-45cc-8886-b21e34101c69","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5719.0,"yMin":-19.0,"xMax":-5504.0,"yMax":88.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player is giving an input, store the direction of that input. 1 is right
      and -1 is left, respective to the camera. If the player is not giving an input,
      set it to 0.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"48b5968f-e3d3-4bdb-b0b1-261afe5e9ba9","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4516.0,"yMin":235.0,"xMax":-4280.0,"yMax":345.0},"title":"Gravity","body":"When
      the player isn''t on the ground, they should accelerate towards it. To do this,
      get the current velocity and the constant gravity, make them into m/timestep,
      and add them up.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"d31392d4-e184-4235-acaf-da82c29901dc","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6962.0,"yMin":13.0,"xMax":-6792.0,"yMax":117.0},"title":"Display
      MaxSpeed","body":"This calculates the max speed of the player based on drag
      and acceleration speed. It is \"displayed\" as an object variable.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"7114167e-fbc2-4585-a9bf-7f5a5cc91fb7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4871.0,"yMin":8.0,"xMax":-4728.0,"yMax":72.0},"title":"Movement","body":"Then
      apply drag to the movement input.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"dbc73ccf-db8a-454a-86f0-fe7a98bdc10e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6419.0,"yMin":-723.0,"xMax":-6232.0,"yMax":-641.0},"title":"Input
      Scale","body":"Scale the player input with respect to physics times and acceleration
      speed.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"8795115f-c03d-4684-bf27-4e1b8d1a08f7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4515.0,"yMin":1108.0,"xMax":-4209.0,"yMax":1232.0},"title":"Dash","body":"Calculate
      how far the player will dash by multiplying the distance by direction (positive
      for right, negative for left, 0 goes nowhere). Then add that to the velocity
      in m/timestep. If the player isn''t giving an input or the character isn''t
      moving, dashing consumes a charge but does nothing.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"04830f34-b424-4a5f-aa67-b0cad8b7dae4","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5541.0,"yMin":-745.0,"xMax":-5351.0,"yMax":-678.0},"title":"Input
      Scale","body":"Add the current velocity in units/timestep to accelerate.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"1e93d8ec-48de-4e41-9571-e54275bd4663","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3914.0,"yMin":-394.0,"xMax":-3724.0,"yMax":-305.0},"title":"Movement","body":"Make
      the player jump by adding the calculated jump force to Motion, then move the
      character with Motion.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"834ea1f1-48c3-4e15-bc28-a7227ac25f7c","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3411.0,"yMin":-91.0,"xMax":-3311.0,"yMax":-1.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player is grounded, don''t move downwards.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"e6ef0479-c3b9-4c19-a9a5-8272e6017139","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7031.0,"yMin":-820.0,"xMax":-6853.0,"yMax":-738.0},"title":"Movement","body":"This
      behemoth controls gravity, drag, and player walking and jumping.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"88859bb0-6601-40da-9ba7-50d08f832800","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6448.0,"yMin":2342.0,"xMax":-6243.0,"yMax":2435.0},"title":"Graveyard","body":"This
      long string is for if I ever want to try making dash defined as a distance
      instead of a force. For now, it is not worth it.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"a08374f4-c50c-4647-b3df-971090c0899b","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4488.0,"yMin":-824.0,"xMax":-4213.0,"yMax":-701.0},"title":"Jump
      Height","body":"To make the player jump a consistent height in m no matter
      what the gravity is.\nThe formula is yVelocity = sqrt(JumpHeight x gravity
      x -2), but there''s a delta time in there because Unity measures most things
      in m/s not timestep.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"2a859ead-85a4-4a70-a75d-40e78d630db7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6830.0,"yMin":996.0,"xMax":-6680.0,"yMax":1073.0},"title":"Other
      Inputs","body":"Tells the graph when the player is trying to jump, dash or
      fastfall.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"95b35221-73b6-46f2-aeb9-91ac3ffda104","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5539.0,"yMin":1158.0,"xMax":-5370.0,"yMax":1295.0},"title":"Dash","body":"First,
      check the player can dash. Make sure they are pushing the button, they haven''t
      dashed the maximum number of times, and they aren''t already dashing.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"59c87fab-90d2-45ae-a177-6b4632295162","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5816.0,"yMin":138.0,"xMax":-5580.0,"yMax":261.0},"title":"Drag","body":"Calculates
      drag, only on the x-axis because combining drag and gravity on y-axis with
      jumping is hard. \nThe formula is velocity / ( 1 + Drag ), with a delta time
      because Unity stores everything in m/s not timestep.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"474c5565-6804-4b2d-8e90-dbf8b51c71d4","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5603.0,"yMin":1894.0,"xMax":-5459.0,"yMax":1969.0},"title":"Grounded
      Check","body":"Check if the player is grounded for gravity and jump reasons.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"0a690392-568a-420a-b5ef-e38c3752a10d","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3224.0,"yMin":-83.0,"xMax":-3033.0,"yMax":-2.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player is not grounded, accelerate them towards the ground.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"91df67b4-f70a-4dec-b0b7-fb7151e53936","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4305.0,"yMin":1296.0,"xMax":-4156.0,"yMax":1361.0},"title":"Dash","body":"Move
      the player with that calculated force.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"cbe3a90b-dc1e-4da6-83c7-1cf2bc14b022","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4314.0,"yMin":2331.0,"xMax":-4131.0,"yMax":2441.0},"title":"Grounded
      Check","body":"If the box finds nothing, the player is not grounded. It is
      still called GravityGrounded from an older version of the jump system.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"be2bcd56-207e-466f-abbe-24ae8351dcbb","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4665.0,"yMin":1998.0,"xMax":-4484.0,"yMax":2107.0},"title":"Grounded
      Check","body":"This lovely node checks if there is anything within the box
      just defined. The Layer Mask means anything not in that layer will be ignored.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"b0759b95-1179-414c-bd47-3ea7a7dd0c0e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4427.0,"yMin":-270.0,"xMax":-4289.0,"yMax":-177.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player is pressing Jump and they haven''t used all their jumps...","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"33222291-ee51-4967-97e4-bbfecbb0635e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5274.0,"yMin":-250.0,"xMax":-5096.0,"yMax":-141.0},"title":"Movement","body":"The
      Motion variable is what eventually gets used to move the player. First, it
      is set to the accelerating movement input.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"a94951ba-ecbe-47d5-967a-037061522762","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3526.0,"yMin":1250.0,"xMax":-3297.0,"yMax":1360.0},"title":"Dash","body":"Run
      a cooldown for the defined amount of time. While it runs, update the cooldown
      percent variable for the indicator. Once it finishes, allow the player to dash
      again.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"2b046fea-6238-4d9e-88ce-befcaf137d75","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4110.0,"yMin":1588.0,"xMax":-3972.0,"yMax":1676.0},"title":"Dash","body":"Add
      a count to the number of dashes and turn off the button input press.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"38657199-a64d-4e77-b97b-7f7a3ee42606","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4315.0,"yMin":1913.0,"xMax":-4089.0,"yMax":2005.0},"title":"Grounded
      Check","body":"If the box finds something, the player is grounded, so stops
      accelerating downwards, and regains all their jumps and dashes.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"1534c3c1-4511-40b9-85b8-a540a687e69b","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3943.0,"yMin":343.0,"xMax":-3744.0,"yMax":432.0},"title":"Gravity","body":"Multiply
      gravity by the FastFall value before adding for acceleration to make it faster
      while the player holds FastFall.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"60da0ed2-fbf7-444f-81a7-adc95399d4fa","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"}],"$version":"A"}}'
